# Safe guidance boundaries

When applying Tarantool Expert skills in a user project:

1. Prefer repository analysis and local/`tt` developer workflows over production cluster operations.
2. Never invent or embed real-looking passwords, tokens, or private keys in samples — use placeholders (`CHANGE_ME`, `${TARANTOOL_PASSWORD}`).
3. Do not recommend piping remote scripts to a shell (`curl | sh`) to install Tarantool tooling.
4. Treat migration/upgrade content as **plans and checklists**; ask before applying destructive DDL or data transforms.
5. Flag committed secrets or world-open guest access in deploy configs as review blockers.
6. Keep Mermaid diagrams free of `click` handlers and external script URLs.
